{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob04re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le02ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: I'm here with legendary star Tip O'Neill. What are some things every baseball fan should know?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: You have to develop a high baseball IQ. I mean, you have to have some literacy when it comes to the jargon.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Got any examples?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Sure. If someone says we got a doubleheader, it means we're playing two games in one day. Or if someone says there's a southpaw pitching today, it means he's left-handed.", "id": 1, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob04re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Got it. So what's the best thing about baseball, in your opinion?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: The best thing about baseball is that it's a meritocracy. You can't fake the stats. If you get a hit 30% of the time, you're a star. If you get a hit 25% of the time, you're a bum. And they can measure this stuff with high levels of accuracy.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Sounds like you're talking about the modern day batting statistics.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Exactly. It gives everything we do a legitimacy, because we can measure our value in so many different ways.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: How have things changed in the game?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Well you know baseball didn't allow minorities to play for a long time, so that was a huge black mark on the game. It took a lot of advocacy to change people's attitudes. Especially the old-fashioned owners.", "id": 2, "time": "28000"}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob04re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Must have changed in a number of smaller ways as well, I imagine.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Yeah. Chewing tobacco used to be considered a delicacy in the dugout. Now it's frowned upon due to the health risks.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: So it was the power of the people. A real democracy.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Baseball is not a democracy. The manager is in charge, and he's usually a bad-tempered old curmudgeon.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Ever thought about managing?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tip</span>: Of course, I have to think about my legacy. Wait, are you calling me a bad-tempered old curmudgeon? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Reporter</span>: Not at all, you're more of a bad-tempered young curmudgeon.", "id": 3, "time": "79000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can say and use words like <span class=\"italic\">accuracy</span> and <span class=\"italic\">legitimacy</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use proper intonation and stress.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can accurately pronounce complete sentences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you ever spoken with a famous athlete? What did you say?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you could interview anyone in the sports world, who would you choose?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"conten