ndary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Stressing Two Syllables Back From the Suffix: -cy", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you say words that end with the suffix -<span class=\"strong\">cy</span>, you stress the third-from-last  syllable from the end of the word, or two syllables before the -<span class=\"strong\">cy </span>ending.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Read these words out loud. Concentrate on the pronunciation. Stress the third-from-last syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "de<span class=\"strong\">mo</span>cracy<br/> <span class=\"strong\">le</span>gacy<br/> meri<span class=\"strong\">to</span>cracy<br/> hy<span class=\"strong\">po</span>crisy", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Of course, I have to think about my legacy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The best thing about baseball is that it's a meritocracy.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Stress for Nouns and Adjectives ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You stress nouns and adjectives in a sentence to add meaning or emphasis to a statement or a message.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In English, 2-syllable adjectives or words usually have stress on the first syllable.<br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">awe</span>some, <span class=\"strong\">pre</span>sent, <span class=\"strong\">cle</span>ver, <span class=\"strong\">foot</span>ball, <span class=\"strong\">base</span>ball</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For compound nouns, the stress is on the first part of the noun.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">green</span>house, <span class=\"strong\">baske</span>tball, v<span class=\"strong\">olley</span>ball</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For compound adjectives, the stress is on the second part of the noun.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">old-<span class=\"strong\">fash</span>ioned, bad-<span class=\"strong\">temp</span>ered</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use an adjective to describe a noun, you normally emphasize the noun if you are not stressing the quality of the noun.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I drive a red <span class=\"strong\">car</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to emphasize the quality of that noun, you stress the adjective that describes it.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look at that <span class=\"strong\">red</span> car over there!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you have several adjectives describing a noun, you stress the quality that you are focusing on the most.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm driving a brand new red <span class=\"strong\">Japanese</span> car. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm here with legendary star Tip O'Neill. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Not at all, you're more of a bad-tempered young curmudgeon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What are some things every baseball fan should know?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "literacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to read and write", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I mean, you have to have some literacy when it comes to the jargon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when conducting an interview with an athlete.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "doubleheader", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when two (usually sporting) events are held in the same day\t", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If someone says we got a doubleheader, it means we're playing two games in one day. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "southpaw", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is left-handed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Or if someone says there's a southpaw pitching today, it means he's left-handed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meritocracy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where everyone is judged on merit and ability", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The best thing about baseball is that it's a meritocracy. You can't fake the stats. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "accuracy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "precision ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They can measure this stuff with high levels of accuracy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "legitimacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the quality of being legal or verified", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It gives everything we do a legitimacy, because we can measure our value in so many different ways.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advocacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "public support of an idea", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It took a lot of advocacy to change people's attitudes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "delicacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a delicious food, usually one that is uncommon and expensive\t", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Chewing tobacco used to be considered a delicacy in the dugout.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dugout", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a shelter, usually located partially underground, for members of a sports team\t", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The visiting team was assigned the eastern dugout.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "legacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what a person leaves behind after moving on or passing away", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Of course, I have to think about my legacy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob04aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose your favorite athlete.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a list of twenty questions to ask.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have a partner read the questions to you. Invent the answers yourself.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research an athlete.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create questions that could be used in an interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I respond to interview questions.", "type": "text"}]}]}